[Music]  welcome to the undiscovered corners of  hotel transylvania from its all-star  voice cast headlined by selena gomez  adam sandler and andy samberg as well as  the lovable monsters and the unique  world they live in the hotel  transylvania films have given us plenty  of spooky silly fun a lot went into  creating this franchise that has won  over the hearts of fans of all ages and  some of it was never even able to reach  the big screen  welcome to hotel transylvania  the opening of hotel transylvania almost  began a couple years earlier an  alternate opening nicknamed love at  first bite featured dracula meeting his  beloved martha and the story of how they  fell in love leading up to the birth of  their daughter mavis while the opening  doesn't go full up and reveal martha's  passing the alternate opening certainly  tugs on the viewer's heartstrings  that being said it's easy to see why  this scene was left on the cutting room  floor as it would have taken away from  the emotional impact of the reveal of  martha's fate later in the film and it  was no mystery who killed her  in a montage that would have played  towards the beginning of the first film  we see several of the monstrous guests  pack up their suitcases and leave their  homes for a relaxing trip to drax hotel  among the travelers are frankenstein and  his wife eunice traveling inside heavy  suitcases from their decaying windmill  home murray sneaking out of his pyramid  a bug-like monster creeping out from the  english sewers and mr foote trying to  blend in with his surroundings during  his travels this scene may be creative  but it simply does not add anything to  the film's plot and was likely cut out  to help make the film's pacing tighter  though this scene did end up making the  teaser trailer  tired of the same old vacation spots  this deleted scene from hotel  transylvania 2 features a commercial for  humans promoting their titular hotel  taking pride in the truce between  monsters and humans the commercial is  hosted by a fly monster who expresses to  a confused human family about how all  the hotel's amenities as well as talking  about how monsters have been integrated  into the human world including griffin  the invisible man hosting a workout  video and mr foote being a star in the  german soccer league while this scene  does serve as some effective exposition  the sequel eventually figures out a more  effective way at letting the audience  know about what has changed since we  last saw the drak pack  this deleted scene from the first hotel  transylvania may have had andy samberg  burst into a rap using his lonely island  cords the scene would have had johnny  offering his take on more modern and hip  music for mavis's 118th birthday with a  wrap that gives a hip-hop spin to the  spooky inhabitants of the titular hotel  as fun as it may have been to see  sandberg bring some of his lonely island  flavor for a scene in the film it's not  hard to see why this did not make the  final product as it doesn't complement  the genuine and sweet nature of the film  as a whole  since murray's voice actor in the first  film was celo green the team behind the  film wanted to put the singer's vocal  chords to good use originally murray was  supposed to have a song and dance number  along with his backup singers known as  the mummettes the actual song that  murray and his bandaged rapt  accompanists would have sung has not  been revealed but it surely had to have  been something spooky  selena gomez has been an active part of  the franchise since the first film in  2012 but before she was cast in the role  another disney channel icon turned  global superstar almost took on the role  of drak's daughter mavis miley cyrus  what cyrus was originally announced to  be voicing the character of mavis but  was eventually fired from the project  after photos surfaced of her doing some  activities that were not particularly  family friendly the studio and cyrus  eventually announced that she would no  longer be voicing mavis and that  replacing her would be gomez looking  back at the movies now gomez definitely  seemed like the perfect fit for the role  they even look alike oh my gosh this is  gonna be so much fun  it's become commonplace for actors to  come and go from the franchise while  singer celo greene initially provides  his voice for the role of marie the  mummy in the first film for the second  third and fourth films he was replaced  by keegan michael key even two of the  biggest marquee names of the hotel  transylvania franchise didn't return for  the fourth film transfermania adam  sandler and kevin james voice actors  brian hull and brad abreal eventually  were cast to replace sandler and james  in the roles of dracula and frankenstein  thankfully hull and abrell are also  impressionists and were able to give  voices that sound almost exactly like  the voices of sandler and james one  wouldn't typically expect family films  populated by kooky and silly monsters to  attempt to strive for accuracy but you  would be surprised the town that the  hotel is located in was directly  influenced by volakia bulgaria the  birthplace of the inspiration behind  dracula vlad the impaler while obviously  there's no real hotel for monsters in  the historical village the film's  architecture is heavily lifted from the  town  mavis and jonathan's precious son dennis  is notable for his poofy red hair but it  was almost even more wild in the  original designs the animation team then  realized the circumference of the  original design for the hair was too big  to even be functional and would have  meant that his parents arms would need  to be double the length in order to even  pick him up this led the animation team  to eventually trim dennis's hair to a  more sustainable look  i got a candy though dennis walking  around with an abnormally large red set  of hair would have been quite amusing to  watch  one of the biggest challenges the hotel  transylvania crew faced while making the  film was animating the kraken at the end  of the third film summer vacation the  team had to build three different  krakens the first being the standard  model the second being one that was  required for when the sea monster  performs the macarena and the third  being what was dubbed a stunticle that  had texture and look dev that would hold  up during close-up shots  much of the zany cast of characters in  the hotel transylvania are directly  inspired by the actors who voice them  the looks of dracula mavis jonathan  frankenstein wayne van helsing and  eunice are directly taken from the  actors who voice them adam sandler  selena gomez andy samberg kevin james  steve buscemi jim gaffigan and fran  drescher no wonder they look so familiar  meanwhile for the other characters such  as murray the mummy and griffin the  invisible man the character design team  had to get a bit more creative  quite a bit went into creating the  character of vlad voiced by the iconic  mel brooks vlad's head shape was  designed to look like a coffin a  callback to the tradition that vampires  sleep in coffins for the aging vampire's  home initially the team debated about  having the character live in a dark and  foreboding castle like something out of  the classic vampire movies ultimately  the team went with a cave to show just  how secluded vlad had become from  civilization you know classic vampire  things  if the legacy cruise ship in the third  film summer vacation looks familiar to  you that's because the ship's design is  directly influenced by the infamous rms  titanic from the ship's black white and  red color scheme to the funnels on the  top the ship clearly resembles the  well-known dreaded ocean liner more so  than the modern ones that the audience  is typically used to  adam sandler is known for including his  real-life family and plenty of his  comedies and that's no different with  hotel transylvania sandler's wife jackie  sandler lended her voice to drock's late  wife martha while his daughters sadie  and sunny sandler have voiced both mavis  as a child as well as wayne and wanda's  werewolf pups the sandlers have to stick  together  since gendi tartovsky has had much  experience with 2d animation he used the  hotel transylvania films to pay tribute  to the tech's avery cartoons that he  grew up with the biggest challenge with  this method was how to take the  organicness of 2d that has no rules  attached and meld it with computer  animation which has more restrictions  the hotel transylvania films have  provided audiences of all ages with  plenty of fun and the franchise has  certainly come a long way since the  first film premiered back in september  of 2012. which hotel transylvania movie  is your favorite

